    description: "WI-tubot prospector run 2026-04-11 found that spring-boot's Kotlin extension functions are flagged as dead code. Example: org.springframework.boot.SpringApplicationExtensions.kt defines fun SpringApplication.with(...)-style Kotlin extension functions. These appear in the dead-code-maybe candidate list with cross_language_hits=8339 because 'with' is a Kotlin stdlib keyword that appears everywhere. The underlying issue is that Kotlin extension-function dispatch is NOT producing a calls edge from receiver.method() call sites to the extension function definition. Root cause hypothesis: the Kotlin analyzer's edge extraction treats 'x.with(...)' as a method call on x's declared type, not as a resolved dispatch to the matching extension function in scope. Fix direction: detect extension-function definitions (funcs with receiver type) and, at edge-extraction time, route any matching call sites to the extension function Symbol. Analogous to how Scala implicit classes and Swift extensions work — likely a shared 'receiver-typed function dispatch' pattern. Scope expansion from prospector finding — priority P3 because Kotlin usage is smaller than Scala/Java in the cohort."  # b339
    fields: {}  # b339
